039911572546, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3700483445103638, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7449005, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Component\\n\\nConfig\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\n\\nAs per the spec:\\n\\n> Setting the [OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk-environment-variables.md#declarative-configuration) environment variable (for languages that support it) provides users a convenient way to initialize OpenTelemetry components without needing to learn language-specific configuration details or use a large number of environment variables. The pattern for accessing the configured components and installing into instrumentation will vary by language. For example, the usage in Java might resemble:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk.md#via-otel_experimental_config_file\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nOpen to suggestions of how this should be implemented to align w/ the rest of the Go SDK implementation\\n\\n### Alternatives\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Prior Art\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Context\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (2)\\n\\n**codeboten** — 2025-10-23T17:18:25Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack descript compon config problem statement a per the spec set the otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk environ variabl md declar configur environ variabl for languag that support it provid user a conveni way to initi opentelemetri compon without need to learn languag specif configur detail or use a larg number of environ variabl the pattern for access the configur compon and instal into instrument will vari by languag for exampl the usag in java might resembl http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk md via otel _ experiment _ config _ file propos solut open to suggest of how this should be implement to align w the rest of the go sdk implement altern _ no respons _ prior art _ no respons _ addit context _ no respons _ sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack discuss 2 codeboten 2025 10 23t17 18 25z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"id\": \"d162a2a65d87b225\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4766339511572546, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3700483445103638, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7253337, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.46691077115725466, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3700483445103638, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6929231, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    - Advantages:\\n\\n      - Avoids SDK import cycles and keeps experimental behavior isolated.\\n\\n      - Lets users opt in; easier to iterate and gather feedback before considering SDK-level integration.\\n\\n- Global vs. explicit provider setup:\\n\\n  - The otel global package has its own subtleties; supporting both code paths may be necessary.\\n\\n  - Global setup increases risk of cycles/complexity; explicit function in contrib is cleaner initially.\\n\\n- Tentative direction:\\n\\n  - Do not add SDK-level support in the short term.\\n\\n  - Prototype in contrib (otelconf); gather user feedback.\\n\\n  - Revisit SDK inclusion later if demand and design stabilize.\\n\\n### Auto-instrumentation considerations\\n\\n- Go auto-instrumentation would likely benefit from config-file-driven setup, but it can build on the contrib implementation once it exists.\\n\\n### SDK experimental features README gap\\n\\n- There is an “observability” feature in an internal X package that is not documented in the README; should be updated.\\n\\n### Metrics pipeline and exponential histogram status\\n\\n- David:\\n\\n  - Working on exponential histogram; close to resolving one remaining issue (race condition).\\n\\n  - Performance is faster but currently ~150 ns vs. a ~120 ns goal; investigating sources of overhead (likely computation).\\n\\n- Tyler:\\n\\n  - Still owes reviews on metrics pipeline optimization PRs.\\n\\n  - Discussed exemplar/histogram locking changes; some PRs shift lock scope; others use a hot/cold structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- Alex: Draft a proposal/PR in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf to:\\n\\n  - Load and apply OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE via an explicit function that returns configured SDK providers.\\n\\n  - Optionally provide an init-based variant guarded by the env var for experimentation (clearly documented).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"advantag avoid sdk import cycl and keep experiment behavior isol let user opt in easier to iter and gather feedback befor consid sdk level integr global v explicit provid setup the otel global packag ha it own subtleti support both code path may be necessari global setup increas risk of cycl complex explicit function in contrib is cleaner initi tentat direct do not add sdk level support in the short term prototyp in contrib otelconf gather user feedback revisit sdk inclus later if demand and design stabil auto instrument consider go auto instrument would like benefit from config file driven setup but it can build on the contrib implement onc it exist sdk experiment featur readm gap there is an observ featur in an intern x packag that is not document in the readm should be updat metric pipelin and exponenti histogram status david work on exponenti histogram close to resolv one remain issu race condit perform is faster but current 150 n v a 120 n goal investig sourc of overhead like comput tyler still owe review on metric pipelin optim pr discuss exemplar histogram lock chang some pr shift lock scope other use a hot cold structur sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol action item alex draft a propos pr in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf to load and appli otel _ experiment _ config _ file via an explicit function that return configur sdk provid option provid an init base variant guard by the env var for experiment clear document\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1109a6ade747ca21\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.38599334403789987, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2572195371969998, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68646556, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"* chore(deps): update module 