7e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"00a9e2d2b5ea8cde\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28312798307722403, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10483182582460579, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69915235, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n`otelhttp` only uses `span.RecordError(err)` when `errType` is not empty\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/otelhttp/transport.go#L132-L140\\n\\nBut `ErrorType` method never returns an empty attribute.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/httptrace/otelhttptrace/internal/semconv/httpconv.go#L443-L458\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI don't have a preference on whether we should record `error.type` with `exception.type` at the same time. But the comment and the logic here seem conflicted. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (15)\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-04-23T08:03:12Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 descript descript otelhttp onli us span recorderror err when errtyp is not empti http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http otelhttp transport go l132 l140 but errortyp method never return an empti attribut http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http httptrace otelhttptrac intern semconv httpconv go l443 l458 expect behavior i don t have a prefer on whether we should record error type with except type at the same time but the comment and the logic here seem conflict sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 discuss 15 dmathieu 2025 04 23t08 03 12z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"67607a2c8d579c3a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2819245486288927, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10240493804127528, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70080364, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.281542978077224, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10483182582460579, \"vector_similarity\": 0.693869, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-